<p>I don’t think it’s a balrog. If I were down in a burning coal mine fleeing for my life from a giant horned fire monster I wouldn’t stick around long enough to get a good look at it, especially since most of its body is probably obscured by smoke anyway. It’d be easy to confused among all the smoke and fire given off by the creature itself and the burning coal around it, so it’s no surprise that reports vary as to its appearance. A LotR fan is already going to expect a balrog when encountering a fire demon in an abandoned mine, so they’ll be more likely to mistake random shapes in the fire and smoke for wings and the iconic weapons. It’s just human pattern recognition at work.</p>

